From c7d028152b9e48b747012b20c2149756fe372134 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jayden Milne <linux@jayd.ml>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 13:50:32 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 10/14] libcamera: software_isp: Pass focus lens controls to
 and from the IPA

To drive a focus lens, the software ISP IPA needs to know the lens
control ranges and to send lens positions back to the pipeline handler.

Pass the lens controls to the IPA at init time, so that it can decide
whether to register the autofocus controls, and at configure time. Add
lens controls to the setSensorControls signal, as done by the IPU3 IPA
interface. The IPA sends a lens control only when the lens has to move,
and the simple pipeline handler applies it immediately, independently
of the sensor controls and of the frame start event.

This follows the approach of Milan Zamazal's autofocus RFC for the
software ISP, without tying lens movements to the presence of a frame
start emitter.

[backport: adapted to the simple IPA of v0.7.2 (src/ipa/simple and
 soft.mojom), which keeps the sensor controls in the IPA class and has
 no lscEnabled output]

Signed-off-by: Jayden Milne <linux@jayd.ml>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
